{"step_index":608,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T07:15:08Z","input_tokens":3011,"cache_read_tokens":110659,"output_tokens":922,"thinking":"The `BLOQUES_ASCII_COMPLETOS_SESION.txt` file's lines 1254-1261 suggest a potential lock state or versioning issue with the download. The `info->unlock_ability = 0` value is particularly concerning and may be the root cause of the observed issues. Investigating the download command and lock state further is necessary to determine if a permissions or version incompatibility is present.\n\n\nThe analysis reveals a locked device state, indicated by `info->lock_state = 1`. Examination of the lock state characters clarifies `info->unlock_ability` is zero due to `lock[2] == '0'`, preventing the unlock command from succeeding. This directly correlates the observed error messages to a feature flag within the device's bootloader. The fastboot unlock command's failure stems from the check `if (info->unlock_ability == 0)`, which bypasses the unlock attempt.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nimport re\ndata = open(r'c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\programa perfecto\\5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\bootloader.img', 'rb').read()\nprint('Size:', len(data))\nfor magic, name in [(b'\\x04\\x22\\x4d\\x18', 'LZ4'), (b'\\x02\\x21\\x4c\\x18', 'LZ4_LEGACY'), (b'\\x1f\\x8b\\x08', 'GZIP'), (b'\\xfd7zXZ\\x00', 'XZ'), (b'\\x89LZO', 'LZO'), (b'@AML', 'AML')]:\n    pos = 0\n    while True:\n        idx = data.find(magic, pos)\n        if idx == -1: break\n        print(f'{name} at 0x{idx:X}')\n        pos = idx + 1\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Find compression headers in bootloader.img"}}]}
